# Byte-exact artifacts.
#
# The SHA-256 of these files is recorded in manifests and verified at runtime by
# the evidence checks and by the judge-demo launcher preflight. That only works
# if the bytes on disk are the bytes in Git on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout. That silently changes every text artifact (a JSON with 91 lines gains
# 91 bytes) and makes every hash comparison fail, so the launcher refuses to
# start and `sync_truth.py --check` cannot pass on a Windows machine.
#
# Pin these paths to LF so a Windows checkout is byte-identical to Linux CI.
docs/evidence/** text eol=lf
apps/web/public/demo/** text eol=lf
apps/web/src/generated/** text eol=lf
services/ml/data/cameroon_61/** text eol=lf

# Point clouds and other binaries must never be line-ending converted or diffed.
*.ply binary
*.las binary
*.laz binary
*.npz binary
*.pt binary

# Office documents are ZIP archives. Git usually detects that on its own, but this
# repository has already lost bytes to autocrlf once, and a single rewritten LF
# inside a ZIP makes the whole file unopenable rather than subtly wrong.
*.docx binary
